# The corpus is the compiler's own emitted assembly, and the peephole kernel
# scans it line by line, so a CRLF checkout would change every line's bytes and
# with them the printed checksum. Pin LF the way *.tl and *.sh are pinned at the
# repository root, so the benchmark's observable output is the same on Linux and
# on the Windows CI runners (whose Git defaults to autocrlf=true).
#
# The file is named .asm rather than .s because the root .gitignore ignores
# *.s (generated assembly), which silently kept this corpus out of the commit.
self-compile.asm text eol=lf
